395	//
396	// THE MONEY FIX. `orderHostingAccount` above debits the WALLET only. First-month-
397	// free (hosting-only) makes a monthly plan $0 for month 1, so the wallet path used
398	// to provision with NOTHING on file — and month-2's renewal had nothing to charge.
399	// `placeHostingOrder` is the wizard's single entry point and closes that gap: it
400	// REFUSES to provision unless the account has a way to bill the renewal (a saved
401	// card OR a wallet balance that already covers one renewal), it is idempotent
402	// against double-submit, and it then delegates the ACTUAL charge to the audited
403	// `orderHostingAccount` above — one debit path, never a second one.
404	//
405	// displayed === charged === renewed: this action computes NO price of its own for
406	// the debit. The wallet debit + the first-month-free reserve→confirm→release
407	// atomicity all live inside `orderHostingAccount`; `renewalCents` here is only the
408	// gate threshold and is the SAME `termPriceCents(plan.priceCents, term, annualPct)`
409	// the renewal sweep charges (worker/product-renewals.ts hostingRenewalPrice).
