I have everything needed. Here's the full mechanics report.

## 1. `components/customer/DeployWizard.tsx`

**Wallet-shortfall gating (`showPaymentStep`) — line ~684:**

```ts
const split = walletSplit({ dueCents, balanceCents, useWallet });
const walletApplied = split.walletApplied;
const cardCents = split.cardCents;
const canDeploy = !!planId && !!imageId && hostnameValid && planMeetsImage;
const isLast = step === steps.length - 1;

// The embedded Payment step only ever replaces the button row for a genuinely
// deployable, card-funded order — never while something else still blocks the
// order, and never for a free/wallet-covered order.
const showPaymentStep = isLast && !free && !primaryBlocker && cardCents > 0;
```

`cardCents` comes straight out of `walletSplit({ dueCents, balanceCents, useWallet })` (`lib/wallet-split.ts`) — that's the single "does wallet cover it" derived value. There's no separate `walletCoversTotal` boolean; `cardCents > 0` **is** the shortfall gate. It's not inserted into a fixed `steps` array as its own step — `Payment` conditionally *replaces the button row* on the last step ("Review") when `showPaymentStep` is true (`{showPaymentStep ? <PaymentStep .../> : <normal Continue/Deploy buttons>}`). When `cardCents <= 0` (wallet fully covers it, or `free`), the ordinary "Deploy — paid from wallet" submit button renders instead and `PaymentStep` never mounts.

**Session-staleness guard** (H2-relevant, line ~631): if the customer changes wallet toggle/coupon *after* a Stripe session is already created, the stamped session is dropped so PaymentStep re-requests a fresh one — never lets them confirm a stale total:

```ts
const prevCardCentsForStripeRef = useRef(cardCents);
useEffect(() => {
  if (checkoutSession && prevCardCentsForStripeRef.current !== cardCents) {
    setCheckoutSession(null);
    setStripePhase("idle");
  }
  prevCardCentsForStripeRef.current = cardCents;
}, [cardCents, checkoutSession]);
```

**Wiring `PaymentStep`'s props (line ~1513):**

```tsx
const [state, action, pending] = useActionState(payAndDeploy, {} as {...});
const [checkoutSession, setCheckoutSession] = useState<{clientSecret; publishableKey} | null>(null);
const [stripePhase, setStripePhase] = useState<"idle"|"loading"|"error">("idle");
const submittedRef = useRef(false);
const formRef = useRef<HTMLFormElement>(null);

const requestStripeSession = useCallback(() => {
  setStripePhase("loading");
  submittedRef.current = true;
  formRef.current?.requestSubmit();   // <-- same <form action={action}> as Deploy
}, []);

useEffect(() => {
  if (submittedRef.current) {
    submittedRef.current = false;
    if (state?.checkout) setCheckoutSession(state.checkout);
    else { setCheckoutSession(null); if (state?.error) setStripePhase("error"); }
  }
}, [state]);
```

```tsx
<PaymentStep
  email={email}
  onBack={() => setStep((s) => Math.max(0, s - 1))}
  stripe={
    checkoutSession
      ? { status: "ready", clientSecret: checkoutSession.clientSecret, publishableKey: checkoutSession.publishableKey }
      : stripePhase === "loading" ? { status: "loading" }
      : stripePhase === "error" ? { status: "error", message: state?.error || "..." }
      : { status: "idle" }
  }
  onRequestStripeSession={requestStripeSession}
  paypal={paypalReady ? { ready: true, clientId: paypalClientId } : null}
  createPayPalOrder={() => createOrderPayPalOrder(new FormData(formRef.current ?? undefined))}
  capturePayPalOrder={(orderId, pendingId) => captureExternalPayPalOrder(orderId, pendingId)}
  coinbaseReady={coinbaseReady}
  createCoinbaseCharge={() => createOrderCoinbaseCharge(new FormData(formRef.current ?? undefined))}
  summary={{ lines: [...], details: [...], billingTermLabel, discountPercent, onChangeTerm,
